{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-10883bef-29a8-46eb-91d3-9c68c782177b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-913ea6d858a43ff0","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-8kzroojx/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-E004.md","content":"# Per-project GPU quota enforcement at admission time\n\n## Description\n\nDeliver per-project GPU quota that is enforced at admission time across\ntraining job types (PyTorchJob and RayJob), so a project's pending and running\ntraining workloads together cannot exceed its GPU quota. This work uses the\nKueue quota model (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue) already shipped in the platform\nand is independent of the gang-admission approach decision: quota is enforced\nby Kueue at admission regardless of post-admission pod scheduling semantics.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define the per-project quota model for GPU resources across training job\n  types, built on the Kueue ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model.\n- Provide the configuration/provisioning mechanism by which each project\n  receives its GPU quota and by which admins adjust it.\n- Ensure both PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads in a project count against the\n  same per-project GPU quota at admission time.\n- Ensure jobs exceeding the project quota remain pending (not partially\n  admitted) until quota is available.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a project with a GPU quota of N, when training jobs (PyTorchJob and\n  RayJob) whose combined GPU request exceeds N are submitted, then jobs are\n  held pending at admission time and no GPU above the quota is occupied.\n- Given two projects, when each submits training jobs, then quota consumption\n  is enforced independently per project.\n- Given an admin changes a project's GPU quota, when new jobs are submitted,\n  then admission follows the updated quota.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): per-project GPU quota enforced at admission time across\n  training job types (PyTorchJob, RayJob).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":39556,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc3876405083066e","agent_id":"a20f64792934626d2","session_id":"175a4578-f41d-49eb-8efd-6ff76cbc31ff","uuid":"5512dadc-34a1-4f6c-8f4e-94e395a66d1f","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:37:37.788Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005"}
