{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-10883bef-29a8-46eb-91d3-9c68c782177b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-becb5f7c98f2e02b","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-8kzroojx/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-E005.md","content":"# Dashboard visibility for pending jobs: queue position, quota consumption, admission state\n\n## Description\n\nExtend the Dashboard so users can see, for their pending training jobs, the\nqueue position, the project's GPU quota consumption, and the admission state.\nThe Dashboard reads Kubernetes CRs and existing queueing metrics and owns no\ndata plane, so this work builds on the queue and quota state the platform\nalready exposes once admission and per-project quota are settled.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add a Dashboard view (or extend the existing distributed workload status\n  views) listing pending training jobs with their queue position and\n  admission state.\n- Surface the project's GPU quota consumption alongside pending jobs,\n  reading the per-project quota model introduced for training workloads.\n- Follow the Dashboard's existing per-component feature-flag and configuration\n  conventions for enabling the new visibility.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a user with pending training jobs in a project, when they open the\n  Dashboard, then they see each pending job's queue position and admission\n  state.\n- Given a project with a per-project GPU quota, when the Dashboard displays\n  pending jobs, then current quota consumption is shown for that project.\n- Given a job transitions from pending to admitted, when the Dashboard view\n  refreshes, then the admission state reflects the change.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1): users can see queue position, quota consumption, and admission\n  state for their pending jobs in the Dashboard.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"sto