{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-10883bef-29a8-46eb-91d3-9c68c782177b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f6173e7d4d23d9b","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-8kzroojx/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-E006.md","content":"# Topology-aware placement preference for training workloads\n\n## Description\n\nDeliver placement that prefers GPU-topology-aligned nodes for training jobs\nwhen the cluster exposes topology information, avoiding placements that cross\nGPU topology domains (e.g. NVLink domains) with significant throughput loss.\nThis epic is gated on the topology discovery maturity assessment: if the\nTech Preview capability is not mature enough to build on this release, this\nepic is removed and the requirement is deferred.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Enable topology-aware placement preference for queued training workloads\n  (PyTorchJob and RayJob) using the platform's topology-aware scheduling\n  capability, respecting the constraints identified by the maturity\n  assessment.\n- Define how placement behaves when topology information is absent (fall\n  back to default placement without error).\n- Validate that representative multi-node training jobs land on\n  topology-aligned nodes when topology information is available.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a cluster exposing GPU topology information, when a multi-node\n  training job is admitted, then its pods are placed preferentially on\n  topology-aligned nodes.\n- Given a cluster that does not expose topology information, when a training\n  job is admitted, then placement falls back to default behavior and the job\n  still runs.\n- Given placements produced with topology preference, when compared to\n  topology-crossing placements, then representative training jobs show no\n  throughput regression from crossing topology domains.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-5 (P2): job placement can prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the\n  cluster exposes topology information.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":39556,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc3876405083066e","agent_id":"a20f64792934626d2","session_id":"175a4578-f41d-49eb-8efd-6ff76cbc31ff","uuid":"fdc73e33-9999-4d8a-a55c-e2af8c5131c3","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:37:55.646Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005"}
