{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92200b0cd10296b6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n3\tepic_count: 6\n4\tcritical_path_length: 2\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9005\n11\t\n12\tQueue-aware GPU scheduling for distributed training workloads.\n13\t\n14\t## Triage\n15\t\n16\tNot below-threshold: the strategy spans three components (Distributed Workloads,\n17\tTraining Operator, Dashboard) and two teams, and contains three open questions\n18\twhose answers change which implementation epics exist or what they do.\n19\tNot documentation-only: all affected components require code/configuration\n20\tchanges. Full decomposition follows.\n21\t\n22\t## Parsed Strategy Structure\n23\t\n24\t- **Affected Components**: Distributed Workloads, Training Operator, Dashboard\n25\t  (no per-component change/owner detail provided — owners taken from\n26\t  architecture context: Distributed Workloads team owns Distributed Workloads\n27\t  and Training Operator; RHOAI Dashboard owns Dashboard).\n28\t- **Impacted Teams table**: MISSING (health warning — owners inferred from\n29\t  architecture context).\n30\t- **High Level Requirements**: HLR-1 (P0, gang admission), HLR-2 (P0,\n31\t  per-project GPU quota at admission), HLR-3 (P1, Dashboard queue/quota/\n32\t  admission visibility), HLR-4 (P1, policy-driven preemption), HLR-5 (P2,\n33\t  topology-aware placement).\n34\t- **Dependencies table**: MISSING (health warning).\n35\t- **Acceptance Criteria**: MISSING as Given/When/Then (health warning — epic\n36\t  ACs derived from HLRs).\n37\t- **Non-Functional Requirements**: MISSING (health warning).\n38\t- **Staff Engineer Input**: absent — no overrides to log.\n39\t\n40\t## Component Graph\n41\t\n42\t| Component | Canonical component | Team | Active/Passive | In platform |\n43\t|-----------|---------------------|------|----------------|-------------|\n44\t| Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | Active (Kueue admission, quota, preemption, placement) | Yes (GA; topology-aware scheduling Tech Preview) |\n45\t| Training Operator | Training Operator | Distributed Workloads | Active (PyTorchJob admission/checkpoint integration) | Yes (GA) |\n46\t| Dashboard | Dashboard | RHOAI Dashboard | Active (HLR-3 user visibility) | Yes (GA) |\n47\t\n48\tAll three components exist in `.context/architecture-context/` and are Konflux\n49\tonboarded — no onboarding chain (repo/konflux/license-validation) is needed.\n50\tComponent names map 1:1 to `.context/rhai-components.txt`; no non-obvious\n51\tmappings. RayJob work lands under the Distributed Workloads component\n52\t(Kueue/KubeRay midstream), PyTorchJob work under Training Operator.\n53\t\n54\t## Epic List (main plan)\n55\t\n56\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n57\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n58\t| E001 | Validate Kueue gang admission for PyTorchJob/RayJob at target scale | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n59\t| E002 | Assess topology-aware scheduling Tech Preview maturity | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | P2 |\n60\t| E003 | Determine required preemption semantics and checkpoint overhead | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | P1 |\n61\t| E004 | Per-project GPU quota enforcement at admission time | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n62\t| E005 | Dashboard visibility for pending jobs: queue position, quota, admission state | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n63\t| E006 | Topology-aware placement preference for training workloads | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P2 |\n64\t\n65\t### Branch epics (conditional, attached to their gating Investigations)\n66\t\n67\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority | Gate |\n68\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|------|\n69\t| BRANCH-A-E007 | Enable Kueue-native gang admission for training workloads | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001, outcome A |\n70\t| BRANCH-A-E008 | Enable PyTorchJob admission integration for gang scheduling | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001, outcome A |\n71\t| BRANCH-B-E007 | Scheduler-plugin gang scheduling (coscheduling) for training workloads | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001, outcome B |\n72\t| BRANCH-B-E008 | Adapt PyTorchJob scheduling for the scheduler-plugin path | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001, outcome B |\n73\t| BRANCH-A-E009 | Policy-driven Kueue preemption with eviction and requeue | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P1 | E003, outcome A |\n74\t| BRANCH-B-E009 | Checkpoint-aware graceful preemption | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P1 | E003, outcome B |\n75\t| BRANCH-B-E010 | PyTorchJob checkpoint support for graceful preemption | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P1 | E003, outcome B |\n76\t\n77\t## Dependency DAG\n78\t\n79\t```mermaid\n80\tgraph TD\n81\t    E001[E001 Investigate gang admission] --> E005[E005 Dashboard visibility]\n82\t    E001 --> E006[E006 Topology-aware placement]\n83\t    E002[E002 Investigate topology maturity] --> E006\n84\t    E004[E004 Per-project GPU quota] --> E005\n85\t    E001 --> BA7[BRANCH-A-E007 Kueue-native gang admission]\n86\t    E001 --> BA8[BRANCH-A-E008 PyTorchJob integration]\n87\t    E001 --> BB7[BRANCH-B-E007 Coscheduling plugin]\n88\t    BB7 --> BB8[BRANCH-B-E008 PyTorchJob plugin adaptation]\n89\t    E003[E003 Investigate preemption semantics] --> BA9[BRANCH-A-E009 Preemption policy + requeue]\n90\t    E003 --> BB9[BRANCH-B-E009 Graceful preemption]\n91\t    E003 --> BB10[BRANCH-B-E010 PyTorchJob checkpoint support]\n92\t    BB10 --> BB9\n93\t```\n94\t\n95\tBranch epics are shown for completeness but are not main-plan nodes; the main\n96\tplan contains E001–E006 only.\n97\t\n98\t## DAG Justification\n99\t\n100\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n101\t|------|------|-----------|\n102\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 3 | What admission state the Dashboard must surface depends on whether admission stays Kueue-native or moves to a scheduler plugin; true gate (`rewrite`). |\n103\t| E001 → E006 | Rule 3 | Placement approach builds on the selected admission path; gate outcome can change scope (`rewrite`). |\n104\t| E002 → E006 | Rule 3 | If topology discovery (Tech Preview) is not mature enough, HLR-5 is deferred — epic may not exist (`remove`). |\n105\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 13 | Dashboard quota-consumption views build against the per-project quota model E004 produces. |\n106\t| E001 → BRANCH-A/B-E007, E008 | Rule 3 | Bounded (2) outcomes of the gang-admission investigation select the branch; conditional decomposition. |\n107\t| BRANCH-B-E007 → BRANCH-B-E008 | Rule 13 | The Training Operator adaptation builds against the plugin's pod-group/gang semantics. |\n108\t| E003 → BRANCH-A/B-E009, BRANCH-B-E010 | Rule 3 | Bounded (2–3) outcomes of the preemption-semantics investigation select the branch; conditional decomposition. |\n109\t| BRANCH-B-E010 → BRANCH-B-E009 | Rule 13 | Checkpoint-aware graceful preemption builds against the PyTorchJob checkpoint capability. |\n110\t| (no edge) E001 → E004 | Rule 14 (independence) | Per-project quota is enforced by Kueue at admission time regardless of post-admission gang semantics; the E001 outcome does not change what E004 does. |\n111\t| (no edge) E004 ∥ branch gang-admission epics | Rule 15 | Different concerns in the same component family; quota model and admission semantics share no build-against artifact. |\n112\t| (no edge) BRANCH-A-E007 ∥ BRANCH-A-E008 | Rule 14 | Different repos (Kueue/KubeRay midstream vs Training Operator midstream), no shared artifact; coordination only. |\n113\t\n114\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n115\t\n116\t| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n117\t|-----|----------|-------|\n118\t| HLR-1 (gang admission, all-or-nothing) | P0 | E001 (investigation), BRANCH-A-E007 + BRANCH-A-E008 (outcome A) or BRANCH-B-E007 + BRANCH-B-E008 (outcome B) |\n119\t| HLR-2 (per-project GPU quota at admission) | P0 | E004 |\n120\t| HLR-3 (Dashboard queue/quota/admission visibility) | P1 | E005 |\n121\t| HLR-4 (policy-driven preemption) | P1 | E003 (investigation), BRANCH-A-E009 (outcome A) or BRANCH-B-E009 + BRANCH-B-E010 (outcome B) |\n122\t| HLR-5 (topology-aware placement) | P2 | E002 (investigation), E006 |\n123\t\n124\tAll five HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements. Priority inheritance:\n125\tE001 inherits P0 (gates all HLR-1 work, which is P0); E003 inherits P1 (HLR-4);\n126\tE002 inherits P2 (HLR-5 only). E005 is P1 and does not push P1 onto E001\n127\t(which is already P0 via HLR-1).\n128\t\n129\t## Conditional Branches\n130\t\n131\t- **E001 (gang admission)** — outcome A: Kueue `waitForPodsReady` satisfies\n132\t  HLR-1 at target scale → BRANCH-A-E007/E008 (enablement/configuration work).\n133\t  Outcome B: insufficient → BRANCH-B-E007/E008 (scheduler-plugin/coscheduling\n134\t  development). The strategy itself states this answer \"changes the shape of\n135\t  most implementation work\", so both HLR-1 implementation slots are branched.\n136\t- **E003 (preemption semantics)** — outcome A: full eviction with requeue\n137\t  suffices → BRANCH-A-E009 (Kueue preemption policy configuration). Outcome B:\n138\t  checkpoint-aware graceful preemption required → BRANCH-B-E009 +\n139\t  BRANCH-B-E010 (checkpoint capability in Training Operator plus graceful\n140\t  preemption in Kueue).\n141\t- **E002 (topology maturity)** — outcome A: mature enough → E006 proceeds\n142\t  (main plan, `gated_by` E002, action `remove`). Outcome B: not mature enough\n143\t  → HLR-5 is deferred to a later release; no branch epics exist for this\n144\t  outcome, so E006 carries a `remove` gate rather than branch files.\n145\t\n146\t## Tiered Delivery\n147\t\n148\tNot applicable as a Tier 1/Tier 2 split: no external community dependency with\n149\tuncertain timing gates user-facing value. All work is in