n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Given the Tech Preview capability's documentation and known issues, when\n51\t  evaluated against the needs of GPU-topology-aligned placement for training\n52\t  workloads, then a go/no-go recommendation is documented with the specific\n53\t  limitations that motivated it.\n54\t- Given a go decision, when the placement implementation starts, then the\n55\t  constraints the implementation must respect (supported topology levels,\n56\t  node types) are enumerated.\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- HLR-5 (P2): job placement preferring GPU-topology-aligned nodes — this\n61\t  investigation determines whether that requirement can be delivered this\n62\t  release.\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-951e480b12557321","agent_id":"ab362f693a2ccaac7","session_id":"175a4578-f41d-49eb-8efd-6ff76cbc31ff","uuid":"3854f307-5673-43a1-9c24-6e511894a079","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:44:08.211Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0479eab1969efbd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
