{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8c84b119f338fa8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E004\n3\ttitle: Per-project GPU quota enforcement at admission time\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Per-project GPU quota enforcement at admission time\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tDeliver per-project GPU quota that is enforced at admission time across\n34\ttraining job types (PyTorchJob and RayJob), so a project's pending and running\n35\ttraining workloads together cannot exceed its GPU quota. This work uses the\n36\tKueue quota model (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue) already shipped in the platform\n37\tand is independent of the gang-admission approach decision: quota is enforced\n38\tby Kueue at admission regardless of post-admission pod scheduling semantics.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Define the per-project quota model for GPU resources across training job\n43\t  types, built on the Kueue ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model.\n44\t- Provide the configuration/provisioning mechanism by which each project\n45\t  receives its GPU quota and by which admins adjust it.\n46\t- Ensure both PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads in a project count against the\n47\t  same per-project GPU quota at admission time.\n48\t- Ensure jobs exceeding the project quota remain pending (not partially\n49\t  admitted) until quota is available.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Given a project with a GPU quota of N, when training jobs (PyTorchJob and\n54\t  RayJob) whose combined GPU request exceeds N are submitted, then jobs are\n55\t  held pending at admission time and no GPU above the quota is occupied.\n56\t- Given two projects, when each submits training jobs, then quota consumption\n57\t  is enforced independently per project.\n58\t- Given an admin changes a project's GPU quota, when new jobs are submitted,\n59\t  then admission follows the updated quota.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-2 (P0): per-project GPU quota enforced at admission time across\n64\t  training job types (PyTorchJob, RayJob).\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-951e480b12557321","agent_id":"ab362f693a2ccaac7","session_id":"175a4578-f41d-49eb-8efd-6ff76cbc31ff","uuid":"f1491a04-1ec9-45cc-9a99-53d464e7d59f","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:44:10.797Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8c84b119f338fa8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
