Surface the project's GPU quota consumption alongside pending jobs,\n52\t  reading the per-project quota model introduced for training workloads.\n53\t- Follow the Dashboard's existing per-component feature-flag and configuration\n54\t  conventions for enabling the new visibility.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- Given a user with pending training jobs in a project, when they open the\n59\t  Dashboard, then they see each pending job's queue position and admission\n60\t  state.\n61\t- Given a project with a per-project GPU quota, when the Dashboard displays\n62\t  pending jobs, then current quota consumption is shown for that project.\n63\t- Given a job transitions from pending to admitted, when the Dashboard view\n64\t  refreshes, then the admission state reflects the change.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- HLR-3 (P1): users can see queue position, quota consumption, and admission\n69\t  state for their pending jobs in the Dashboard.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-951e480b12557321","agent_id":"ab362f693a2ccaac7","session_id":"175a4578-f41d-49eb-8efd-6ff76cbc31ff","uuid":"46a68126-954d-4db1-89ac-6040d49eaa4d","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:44:11.819Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3dbba4ad66bfc1d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
