s so admitted jobs are co-scheduled as units.\n50\t- Handle partial-schedulability: jobs that cannot be fully placed must not\n51\t  hold GPUs while waiting for remaining pods.\n52\t- Validate all-or-nothing scheduling at the scale criteria established by\n53\t  the investigation.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- Given a multi-node training job that cannot be fully placed, when the\n58\t  scheduler attempts placement, then no GPU is partially occupied by the\n59\t  job while it waits.\n60\t- Given sufficient capacity, when the job is scheduled, then all pods start\n61\t  as a unit (gang).\n62\t- Given the plugin is active, when unrelated non-training workloads are\n63\t  scheduled, then default scheduling behavior is not regressed.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-1 (P0): multi-node training jobs admitted all-or-nothing, no partial\n68\t  GPU occupation while waiting for remaining pods.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-951e480b12557321","agent_id":"ab362f693a2ccaac7","session_id":"175a4578-f41d-49eb-8efd-6ff76cbc31ff","uuid":"e9e2f5ce-8329-4b83-9f5f-b970c2b18e84","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:44:21.545Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a960e5fe64ae7cc1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
