{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8c1700fbe57e57d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E009\n3\ttitle: Policy-driven Kueue preemption with eviction and requeue\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E003\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E003\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the preemption investigation requires checkpoint-aware graceful\n16\t    preemption, this policy-configuration work is rewritten as graceful preemption\n17\t    orchestration plus training-job checkpoint support.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 1\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 0\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 6\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Policy-driven Kueue preemption with eviction and requeue\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tBranch A of the preemption implementation (applies when the preemption\n39\tsemantics investigation concludes that full eviction with requeue satisfies\n40\tcustomer needs): configure policy-driven preemption in the queueing layer so\n41\thigher-priority workloads preempt lower-priority ones according to an\n42\tadmin-defined policy, with preempted jobs requeued rather than checkpointed.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Expose admin-defined preemption policy configuration (which workloads may\n47\t  preempt which, and requeue behavior) on the platform's queueing\n48\t  configuration.\n49\t- Ensure preempted jobs are evicted fully (no partial GPU occupation left\n50\t  behind) and requeued for later re-admission.\n51\t- Validate preemption behavior with mixed-priority training workloads\n52\t  (PyTorchJob and RayJob).\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Given an admin-defined preemption policy, when a higher-priority workload\n57\t  is admitted, then lower-priority workloads are preempted per the policy.\n58\t- Given a preempted job, when eviction completes, then all its GPUs are\n59\t  released and the job is requeued (no partial occupation).\n60\t- Given a requeued preempted job, when capacity becomes available, then it\n61\t  is re-admitted and restarted.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- HLR-4 (P1): higher-priority workloads can preempt lower-priority ones\n66\t  according to an admin-defined policy.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-951e480b12557321","agent_id":"ab362f693a2ccaac7","session_id":"175a4578-f41d-49eb-8efd-6ff76cbc31ff","uuid":"fe90d2ac-075c-4cd8-b42d-d4b402990e65","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:44:23.152Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8c1700fbe57e57d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
