n52\t  checkpoint support) so progress is captured and restored for multi-node\n53\t  jobs.\n54\t- Make graceful versus plain eviction selectable through the admin-defined\n55\t  preemption policy.\n56\t- Validate checkpoint overhead in practice against the benchmark produced by\n57\t  the preemption semantics investigation.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- Given a running training job is preempted under a graceful-preemption\n62\t  policy, when preemption occurs, then a checkpoint is taken before eviction\n63\t  and all GPUs are released.\n64\t- Given the preempted job is requeued and re-admitted, when it restarts, then\n65\t  it resumes from the checkpoint rather than starting from scratch.\n66\t- Given an admin-defined policy that selects plain eviction, when\n67\t  preemption occurs, then behavior matches full-eviction-with-requeue\n68\t  semantics.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-4 (P1): higher-priority workloads can preempt lower-priority ones\n73\t  according to an admin-defined policy, with checkpoint-aware graceful\n74\t  semantics.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-951e480b12557321","agent_id":"ab362f693a2ccaac7","session_id":"175a4578-f41d-49eb-8efd-6ff76cbc31ff","uuid":"4d431ec6-9bc4-4c43-b379-94182a8fa240","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:44:31.367Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2a0a73be8e0f75c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
