{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a98ba9846fbc2da","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate Kueue gang admission for PyTorchJob/RayJob at target scale\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Validate Kueue gang admission for PyTorchJob/RayJob at target scale\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's first open question: whether Kueue's\n30\tcurrent gang-admission semantics (`waitForPodsReady`) actually satisfy the\n31\tall-or-nothing admission requirement for multi-node PyTorchJob and RayJob\n32\tworkloads at the platform's target scale, or whether scheduler-plugin work\n33\t(e.g. coscheduling) beyond Kueue is required. The strategy explicitly states\n34\tthat this answer changes the shape of most implementation work, so all gang\n35\tadmission implementation epics are gated on this outcome.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Define the concrete \"target scale\" criteria (nodes, GPUs, concurrent mixed\n40\t  jobs) that the validation must satisfy — the strategy references target\n41\t  scale without defining it.\n42\t- Study Kueue's admission and `waitForPodsReady` semantics from source and\n43\t  documentation, including known failure modes for partial pod occupation and\n44\t  timeout behavior.\n45\t- Exercise PyTorchJob and RayJob admission through Kueue locally and on a\n46\t  shared cluster at the defined scale, observing whether GPUs are ever\n47\t  partially occupied while a job waits for remaining pods.\n48\t- Produce a decision document with one of two bounded outcomes:\n49\t  - **Outcome A**: Kueue-native semantics satisfy the all-or-nothing\n50\t    requirement; implementation proceeds as configuration/integration\n51\t    enablement.\n52\t  - **Outcome B**: Kueue-native semantics are insufficient; scheduler-plugin\n53\t    (e.g. coscheduling) work is required.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- Given a defined target-scale scenario, when a multi-node PyTorchJob and a\n58\t  RayJob are submitted under contention, then it is determined and documented\n59\t  whether any GPU is held by a partially admitted job while remaining pods\n60\t  are pending.\n61\t- Given the validation results, when a timeout or eviction of a partially\n62\t  scheduled job occurs, then the observed behavior against the\n63\t  no-partial-occupation requirement is documented with reproductions.\n64\t- A decision document records outcome A or B, the evidence, and the scale\n65\t  criteria used, so the gated implementation epics can start.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-1 (P0): multi-node training jobs admitted all-or-nothing — this\n70\t  investigation determines the implementation approach that will deliver it.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-857554a6646b13bf","agent_id":"a84cee474f1f50b90","session_id":"175a4578-f41d-49eb-8efd-6ff76cbc31ff","uuid":"1acbf2bd-bbdc-4334-8666-f6a216ad33d2","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:52:08.853Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a98ba9846fbc2da","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
