{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-afd7b8e5921fbc59","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9005\n3\ttitle: Queue-aware GPU scheduling for distributed training workloads\n4\tstatus: Refinement Done\n5\tpriority: Critical\n6\tlabels:\n7\t- refined\n8\tlinks: []\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## Problem Statement\n12\t\n13\tLarge training jobs fail or waste capacity because pods are admitted piecemeal:\n14\ta 16-GPU job can hold 12 GPUs for hours waiting for the last 4, starving other\n15\tteams, and partially scheduled jobs die on timeout. Customers running mixed\n16\tfleets also report that jobs land on suboptimal GPU topologies (crossing NVLink\n17\tdomains) with significant throughput loss. We need admission and placement that\n18\ttreats a multi-node training job as one unit and uses GPU topology where it\n19\tmatters.\n20\t\n21\t## High-Level Requirements\n22\t\n23\t| ID | Priority | Requirement |\n24\t|-------|----------|-------------|\n25\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing: no partial GPU occupation while waiting for remaining pods. |\n26\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Per-project GPU quota is enforced at admission time across training job types (PyTorchJob, RayJob). |\n27\t| HLR-3 | P1 | Users can see queue position, quota consumption, and admission state for their pending jobs in the Dashboard. |\n28\t| HLR-4 | P1 | Higher-priority workloads can preempt lower-priority ones according to an admin-defined policy. |\n29\t| HLR-5 | P2 | Job placement can prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the cluster exposes topology information. |\n30\t\n31\t## Affected Components\n32\t\n33\t- Distributed Workloads\n34\t- Training Operator\n35\t- Dashboard\n36\t\n37\t## Out of Scope\n38\t\n39\t- GPU sharing/fractioning (MIG, time-slicing policy management)\n40\t- Cross-cluster or multi-cluster queueing\n41\t\n42\t## Open Questions\n43\t\n44\t1. Do Kueue's current gang-admission semantics (waitForPodsReady) actually\n45\t   satisfy HLR-1 for PyTorchJob and RayJob at our target scale, or do we need\n46\t   scheduler-plugin work (e.g. coscheduling) beyond Kueue? The answer changes\n47\t   the shape of most implementation work.\n48\t2. Topology-aware placement (HLR-5) depends on node topology discovery that is\n49\t   only Tech Preview — is it mature enough to build on this release?\n50\t3. What preemption semantics do reference customers actually need — full\n51\t   eviction with requeue, or checkpoint-aware graceful preemption? We have\n52\t   conflicting field signals and no benchmark of checkpoint overhead.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e132ce62e656773","agent_id":"a68d4b19d59b431d6","session_id":"175a4578-f41d-49eb-8efd-6ff76cbc31ff","uuid":"54234f64-51ff-4efd-a769-3043510cbdbf","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:55:55.420Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-afd7b8e5921fbc59","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005"}
