{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a282f7f0ebc37dad","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E007\n3\ttitle: Enable Kueue-native gang admission for training workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the gang-admission investigation finds Kueue-native semantics\n16\t    insufficient, this enablement work is rewritten as scheduler-plugin (coscheduling)\n17\t    development.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 1\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 8\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Enable Kueue-native gang admission for training workloads\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tBranch A of the gang-admission implementation (applies when the gang-admission\n39\tinvestigation concludes that Kueue's native semantics satisfy the\n40\tall-or-nothing requirement at target scale): enable and configure Kueue-native\n41\tgang admission so multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing, with\n42\tno partial GPU occupation while waiting for remaining pods.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Configure Kueue admission (waitForPodsReady semantics) for training\n47\t  workloads so a job's pods are admitted as a unit.\n48\t- Enable gang admission for RayJob workloads through the Kueue/KubeRay\n49\t  integration in the platform's midstream queueing components.\n50\t- Tune admission timeout/requeue behavior for partially schedulable jobs so\n51\t  they do not hold GPUs while waiting for remaining pods.\n52\t- Validate all-or-nothing admission for multi-node jobs under contention at\n53\t  the scale criteria established by the investigation.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- Given a 16-GPU job of which only 12 GPUs are currently available, when the\n58\t  job is submitted, then it remains fully pending and holds no GPUs.\n59\t- Given a multi-node RayJob and PyTorchJob under queue contention, when\n60\t  admitted, then all pods start together or the job is requeued.\n61\t- Given jobs that cannot be fully admitted within the configured timeout,\n62\t  when the timeout expires, then they are evicted/requeued without leaving\n63\t  partial GPU occupation.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-1 (P0): multi-node training jobs admitted all-or-nothing, no partial\n68\t  GPU occupation while waiting for remaining pods.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e132ce62e656773","agent_id":"a68d4b19d59b431d6","session_id":"175a4578-f41d-49eb-8efd-6ff76cbc31ff","uuid":"ba70b443-6568-42ac-ba0b-db800fb84b28","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:56:12.017Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a282f7f0ebc37dad","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005"}
