ontention,\n51\t  jointly with the queueing-side enablement work.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Given a multi-node PyTorchJob submitted to a queue with insufficient\n56\t  capacity, when it is pending, then none of its pods occupy GPUs.\n57\t- Given sufficient capacity, when the job is admitted, then all worker pods\n58\t  start as a unit.\n59\t- Given the integration is enabled, when existing PyTorchJob behavior is\n60\t  regression-tested, then non-queued jobs continue to run unchanged.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-1 (P0): multi-node training jobs admitted all-or-nothing (PyTorchJob\n65\t  side).\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e132ce62e656773","agent_id":"a68d4b19d59b431d6","session_id":"175a4578-f41d-49eb-8efd-6ff76cbc31ff","uuid":"c5002d6f-c869-4e77-803c-f913148f0b99","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:56:13.084Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aad9363bcbfd8b1f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005"}
