{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95af8bfd527cb5d2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E007\n3\ttitle: Scheduler-plugin gang scheduling (coscheduling) for training workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the gang-admission investigation finds Kueue-native semantics\n16\t    sufficient, this scheduler-plugin work is dropped in favor of Kueue-native enablement.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: -1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n21\t  existing_foundation: 0\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 0\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 0\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Scheduler-plugin gang scheduling (coscheduling) for training workloads\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tBranch B of the gang-admission implementation (applies when the gang-admission\n38\tinvestigation concludes that Kueue's native semantics do NOT satisfy the\n39\tall-or-nothing requirement at target scale): implement gang scheduling for\n40\ttraining workloads (PyTorchJob and RayJob) via scheduler-plugin work\n41\t(e.g. coscheduling) beyond Kueue, so multi-node jobs are scheduled\n42\tall-or-nothing.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Design and integrate a scheduler-plugin gang scheduling capability (e.g.\n47\t  coscheduling pod groups) for the platform's training workloads, based on\n48\t  the failure evidence gathered by the investigation.\n49\t- Ensure RayJob workloads, through the Kueue/KubeRay integration in the\n50\t  platform's midstream queueing components, participate in the plugin's gang\n51\t  scheduling path alongside PyTorchJob.\n52\t- Wire the queueing layer's admission decisions to the plugin's gang\n53\t  scheduling semantics so admitted jobs are co-scheduled as units.\n54\t- Handle partial-schedulability: jobs that cannot be fully placed must not\n55\t  hold GPUs while waiting for remaining pods.\n56\t- Validate all-or-nothing scheduling at the scale criteria established by\n57\t  the investigation.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- Given a multi-node training job that cannot be fully placed, when the\n62\t  scheduler attempts placement, then no GPU is partially occupied by the\n63\t  job while it waits.\n64\t- Given sufficient capacity, when a multi-node RayJob or PyTorchJob is\n65\t  scheduled, then all pods start as a unit (gang).\n66\t- Given the plugin is active, when unrelated non-training workloads are\n67\t  scheduled, then default scheduling behavior is not regressed.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-1 (P0): multi-node training jobs admitted all-or-nothing, no partial\n72\t  GPU occupation while waiting for remaining pods.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e132ce62e656773","agent_id":"a68d4b19d59b431d6","session_id":"175a4578-f41d-49eb-8efd-6ff76cbc31ff","uuid":"523088a3-11cb-40b9-b874-d9bd3eab3dc7","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:56:15.481Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-95af8bfd527cb5d2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005"}
