{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b93b679379a08e03","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E009\n3\ttitle: Checkpoint-aware graceful preemption\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E003\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E003\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E010\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the preemption investigation finds full eviction with requeue\n17\t    sufficient, the graceful-preemption work is dropped and preemption is delivered\n18\t    as policy-driven eviction with requeue.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: -1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 0\n25\t  external_dependency: -1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 0\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 0\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Checkpoint-aware graceful preemption\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tBranch B of the preemption implementation (applies when the preemption\n40\tsemantics investigation concludes that checkpoint-aware graceful preemption\n41\tis required): implement graceful preemption in the queueing layer so that\n42\twhen a higher-priority workload preempts a running training job, the job's\n43\tprogress is checkpointed before eviction and restored after requeue, per the\n44\tadmin-defined policy.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Implement graceful preemption orchestration in the queueing layer:\n49\t  trigger a checkpoint before eviction, evict, requeue, and restore from the\n50\t  checkpoint on re-admission.\n51\t- Integrate with the training-job checkpoint capability (PyTorchJob\n52\t  checkpoint support) so progress is captured and restored for multi-node\n53\t  jobs.\n54\t- Make graceful versus plain eviction selectable through the admin-defined\n55\t  preemption policy.\n56\t- Validate checkpoint overhead in practice against the benchmark produced by\n57\t  the preemption semantics investigation.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- Given a running training job is preempted under a graceful-preemption\n62\t  policy, when preemption occurs, then a checkpoint is taken before eviction\n63\t  and all GPUs are released.\n64\t- Given the preempted job is requeued and re-admitted, when it restarts, then\n65\t  it resumes from the checkpoint rather than starting from scratch.\n66\t- Given an admin-defined policy that selects plain eviction, when\n67\t  preemption occurs, then behavior matches full-eviction-with-requeue\n68\t  semantics.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-4 (P1): higher-priority workloads can preempt lower-priority ones\n73\t  according to an admin-defined policy, with checkpoint-aware graceful\n74\t  semantics.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e132ce62e656773","agent_id":"a68d4b19d59b431d6","session_id":"175a4578-f41d-49eb-8efd-6ff76cbc31ff","uuid":"f33ed3bd-7306-423f-8882-71f97660bcb8","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:56:17.692Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b93b679379a08e03","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005"}
