ter eviction.\n52\t- Validate multi-node PyTorchJob all-or-nothing scheduling under contention\n53\t  jointly with the scheduler-plugin work.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- Given a multi-node PyTorchJob managed by the plugin path, when capacity is\n58\t  insufficient, then none of its pods occupy GPUs while pending.\n59\t- Given the job is gang-scheduled, when workers start, then all pods start\n60\t  as a unit and training proceeds.\n61\t- Given an evicted/requeued PyTorchJob, when it is rescheduled, then it\n62\t  restarts cleanly.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-1 (P0): multi-node training jobs admitted all-or-nothing (PyTorchJob\n67\t  side under the scheduler-plugin path).\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e132ce62e656773","agent_id":"a68d4b19d59b431d6","session_id":"175a4578-f41d-49eb-8efd-6ff76cbc31ff","uuid":"b9614eef-19fb-4148-9a36-8d2efe6c0ea3","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:56:24.958Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9427241e38510808","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005"}
