sistent.\n\nLet me also double-check the local_runnability rubric for E001: \"+1 the components can be exercised as a downloaded binary or pip/npm library locally\". Kueue/training-operator/kuberay controllers run as binaries against a local API server — rationale is defensible. cluster_hardware_dependence -2: \"a gating question does [need live cluster/GPU/prod-scale]\" — the gating question is \"at target scale\", so -2 justified. ✓\n\nE002 local_runnability 0: topology discovery requires GPU nodes — correct, can't run locally. ✓ chd -1: core from public record, confirming on GPU nodes needs cluster — peripheral. ✓ hjr -1: risk acceptance is a product call — peripheral stakeholder decision. ✓\n\nE003: qs 0 — \"what do reference customers actually need\" has no defined pass/fail until field input — reasonable (not -1 because the two candidate semantics are enumerable and benchmark measurable — middling, 0 defensible). sa 0 — customer needs live in field signals, not readable artifacts — matches the \"0 when the only readable material does not hold the answer\" condition exactly. hjr -2 — gating question requires customer input — matches. lr 1 — benchmark runs locally with pip-installed frameworks — defensible. chd -1 — realistic gang pressure needs cluster — peripheral. ✓\n\nE005 open_questions -1: gated on E001 — \"open questions that would change implementation approach\" — which admission states to surface depends on E001 outcome. ✓ consistent.\n\nE006 signals all consistent.\n\nBranch signal checks:\n- A-E007 cs 1: \"Kueue's admission knobs... documented, named APIs\" — the strategy says \"Configure Kueue admission (waitForPodsReady)\". Change specificity +1 requires \"exact file paths, API endpoints, field names known\". waitForPodsReady is a named API field. Defensible. oq 1: gating question resolved in its favor — matches \"all design decisions resolved for this epic\"? There's some tension: within branch A, the work is configuration on known surfaces. Defensible.\n- B-E007 ed -1: \"Likely requires upstream scheduler-plugins work or OpenShift scheduler coordination\" — plausible.\n- B-E009 ed -1: \"If upstream Kueue lacks graceful preemption hooks, this likely requires an upstream contribution\" — plausible.\n\nNow, one point to scrutinize: E001's `human_judgment_required: 0` — the outcome is empirical. ✓. E002 hjr -1 ✓.\n\nOne more possible issue: A-E008 external_dependency 0 vs A-E007 ed 1 — A-E008 rationale \"small upstream fixes cannot be ruled out — neutral\". Fine, judgment call, not a contradiction.\n\nNow let me check the architecture context files to validate component existence, teams, and key claims (Kueue waitForPodsReady, topology-aware Tech Preview, Dashboard reads CRs).","signature":"5f6f25c3abbd4f6798951d4bfcdb690b"}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50963,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e132ce62e656773","agent_id":"a68d4b19d59b431d6","session_id":"175a4578-f41d-49eb-8efd-6ff76cbc31ff","uuid":"4ec566f8-4199-4ba2-8874-c62d084f0854","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:00:25.546Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005"}
